# ============================================================
#  Crises: queued by resources hitting zero (see core/rules.grim)
#  and by debt. These are the "game over" gates — each gives the
#  player one way out, at a price, before ending the run.
# ============================================================

@event crisis_collapse
title: Collapse
trigger: queued
priority: 90
art: cross
tags: crisis
scene: A narrow infirmary bed under a high arched window, a healer's lamp floating beside it.
text: The world tilts. When it rights itself you are in the infirmary, and Sister Amaranth is looking at you over her spectacles. "You have been running your body like a borrowed broom," she says.
> left: Pay for the full cure (30 gold)
  if gold >= 30:
    gold -30
    health +40
    say: Three foul tonics and two days' sleep later, you feel almost human.
  elif collapses >= 1:
    end ending_sent_home
  else:
    health +20
    grades -8
    collapses += 1
    say: You can't pay. She heals you anyway, slowly, and you miss a fortnight of classes.
> right: Ask to rest instead
  if collapses >= 1:
    end ending_sent_home
  else:
    health +25
    grades -10
    mood -5
    collapses += 1
    lose sick
    say: A long, dull fortnight in bed. Sister Amaranth warns you: "Next time, I write to your family."

@event crisis_despair
title: The Grey
trigger: queued
priority: 90
art: rain
tags: crisis
scene: A student sitting on the edge of a dormitory bed, rain on the window, a packed trunk by the door.
text: Everything has gone grey. You have packed your trunk twice this week and unpacked it once. It would be so easy to take the next barge and simply stop.
> left: Reach out to someone
  if bonds(friend) + bonds(close) + bonds(partner) > 0:
    mood +30
    say: You knock on a friend's door. They don't ask questions. They just make tea, and stay.
  elif met(maud):
    mood +20
    rel maud +6
    say: Old Maud finds you in the gardens and puts a trowel in your hand. "Dig," she says. You dig. It helps more than it should.
  elif despairs >= 1:
    end ending_quiet_departure
  else:
    mood +15
    despairs += 1
    say: You talk to the night porter, of all people. He tells you about his own first year. It's enough, for now.
> right: Take the next barge
  if despairs >= 1:
    end ending_quiet_departure
  else:
    mood +12
    despairs += 1
    say: You get as far as the landing. The barge is late. By the time it arrives, you have decided to stay one more month.

@event crisis_probation
title: The Disciplinary Board
trigger: queued
priority: 90
art: scales
tags: crisis
scene: Three faculty members behind a high bench in a dim chamber; the headmistress in the centre, hands folded.
text: Your standing has collapsed. You are summoned before the Disciplinary Board: three professors and the headmistress, who looks at you with an expression of deep, patient disappointment.
> left: Plead your case (Charm)
  if has(probation):
    end ending_expelled
  else:
    check charm 25:
      grades +20
      gain probation
      say: You speak honestly and well. They grant you probation. "Do not make us regret it."
    else:
      grades +12
      gain probation
      mood -8
      say: You stammer. They grant probation anyway, but the headmistress's sigh will haunt you.
> right: Promise to work harder
  if has(probation):
    end ending_expelled
  else:
    grades +15
    gain probation
    mood -5
    say: "Promises are cheap," says Professor Thorne. "We'll take it anyway." Probation.

@event grisk_collectors
title: Grisk's Collectors
trigger: queued
priority: 80
art: chain
tags: crisis money
chain: debt
scene: Two large trolls in ill-fitting waistcoats looming in a dormitory doorway, one holding a ledger.
text: Two trolls in waistcoats are waiting outside your dormitory. "Mister Grisk," says the larger one, "is disappointed." The smaller one cracks his knuckles, which sounds like a rockslide.
> left: Hand over everything you have
  gold = 0
  debt_missed = 0
  mood -6
  if debt_paid >= 3:
    lose in_debt
    say: They count your purse twice and declare the debt settled. "Pleasure," says the large one, meaning it.
  else:
    debt_paid += 2
    say: They take every coin and your good boots. "Partial," they say, and leave.
> right: Run
  check vigor 22:
    debt_missed = 1
    mood -2
    say: You escape across the rooftops. They'll be back, but not this month.
  else:
    health -18
    debt_missed = 0
    say: You do not escape. The trolls are surprisingly gentle about breaking only one rib.
    gain injured
